all the workers of vain striving of iniquity no knowledge,","poem":1},{"text":"who eat up my people as they eat bread,","poem":2},{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"and don’t call on Adonai?","poem":2}]},{"type":"verse","number":5,"content":[{"text":"There they were in great fear,","poem":1},{"text":"for God is in the generation of the upright.","poem":2}]},{"type":"verse","number":6,"content":[{"text":"You frustrate the plan of the poor,","poem":1},{"text":"because Adonai is his refuge.","poem":2}]},{"type":"verse","number":7,"content":[{"text":"Oh that the yishu'ah ·salvation· of Israel [God prevails] would come out of Zion [Mountain ridge, Marking]!","poem":1},{"text":"When Adonai restores the fortunes of his people,","poem":2},{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"then Jacob [Supplanter] shall rejoice, and Israel [God prevails] shall be glad.","poem":2}]},{"type":"line_break"}],"footnotes":[{"noteId":30,"caller":"+","text":". (1-3) Quoted in  Rom 3:10-12","reference":{"chapter":14,"verse":3}}]},"thisChapterLink":"/api/eng_our/PSA/14.json","thisChapterAudioLinks":{},"nextChapterApiLink":"/api/eng_our/PSA/15.json","nextChapterAudioLinks":{},"previousChapterApiLink":"/api/eng_our/PSA/13.json","previousChapterAudioLinks":{},"numberOfVerses":7}